====
There are 3 main stages

1. Train in SageMaker

Your training data can be in:

S3
 ↓
SageMaker Training Job
 ↓
Random Forest / other ML algorithm
 ↓
model.tar.gz

===

2. Deploy in SageMaker

model.tar.gz
 ↓
SageMaker Model
 ↓
SageMaker Endpoint

For your project, this could be:

insurance-charge-endpoint4

====

3. Call the endpoint from VS Code

Your local aws.py does:

predictor.predict(input_data)

and SageMaker returns something like:

Predicted Insurance Charge:  XXXXX

====

Important distinction

Your VS Code does NOT need to train the model in this setup.

| Activity           | Location         |
| ------------------ | ---------------- |
| Store dataset      | AWS S3           |
| Train ML model     | AWS SageMaker    |
| Save trained model | AWS SageMaker/S3 |
| Deploy model       | AWS SageMaker    |
| Run endpoint       | AWS SageMaker    |
| Send prediction    | Local VS Code    |
| Display prediction | Local VS Code    |


====



